Add({
	id = "blasted-lands",
	title = "Blasted Lands",
	faction = "Contested",
	continent = "Eastern Kingdoms",
	maps = { 1419, 17 },
	zone = "Blasted Lands",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
		{ type = "map" },
	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Blasted Lands lie at the southern end of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}, below the {link:swamp-of-sorrows}Swamp of Sorrows{/link}. Nothing green grows there. The earth is red as a wound and the hills are bare. The sky flickers with lightning that brings no rain. At the southern end of this desert stands the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, the gate through which the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} first came into the world. The gate is dark and silent now. Yet the land around it has never healed. {link:ogres}Ogres{/link}, demons and cultists have made it their own, and a single fortress of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} keeps watch on the road.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Before the orcs came, this country was the southern part of the Black Morass, a dark fen that ran south from the swamps. It was there that the warlock {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link} and the Guardian {link:medivh}Medivh{/link} opened their gate between the worlds, and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} marched out of the mire to fall upon the kingdom of {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Stormwind{/link}. The fel magic that raised the Portal poisoned the marsh around it. When the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} broke the gate at the end of the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the land suffered a second wound. The water died, the reeds withered, and the soil burned to the color it bears today. The folk of the kingdoms gave the ruined country a plain and bitter name, and it has kept that name ever since.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Portal has been quiet for many years, but the Blasted Lands have not been quiet with it. After the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} was broken at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, a remnant of its host withdrew into the {link:the-tainted-scar}Tainted Scar{/link} in the south-west, under the doom lord {link:lord-kazzak}Kazzak{/link}. His lieutenant, the demon {link:razelikh-the-defiler}Razelikh the Defiler{/link}, has spent the years since binding the land's other powers to himself. The cultists of the Shadowsworn serve him. So do the Dreadmaul ogres, whose chieftain is now more demon than {link:ogres}ogre{/link}. Some of the lost draenei wander the wastes, seeking a way home. At the northern edge of it all stands {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde Keep{/link}, where the magi of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} and the soldiers who guard them study the Portal and wait for the day it wakes. The road to the keep is long, and the caravans that feed it do not always arrive.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The watchers of {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde{/link}.{/b} Magi, clerics, soldiers and miners hold the keep and its mines in the northern hills. They are few, and they are a long way from home.
• {b}The Dreadmaul ogres.{/b} The Dreadmaul hold the north-west of the wastes and roam its centre. Their warlocks and {link:ogres}ogre{/link} magi have learned dark arts from their demonic master.
• {b}The Shadowsworn.{/b} These cultists hold the caves of the {link:serpent-s-coil}Serpent's Coil{/link} and the Altar of Storms in the west. They are the heirs of the old {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}, and they serve {link:razelikh-the-defiler}the Defiler{/link}.
• {b}The {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}.{/b} Doomguard, dreadlords, felguards and felhounds haunt the {link:the-tainted-scar}Tainted Scar{/link} and the approaches of the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}.
• {b}The lost draenei.{/b} Wretched exiles of an ancient people wander the land. Some are mad, and some still hope.
• {b}The beasts of the waste.{/b} Hyenas, basilisks, scorpoks, vultures and great boars have grown strong and strange in the tainted earth.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Black Morass.{/b} No chronicle tells how long the fen lay undisturbed before the orcs came. It was remote, wet and all but empty of people.
• {b}The First War.{/b} The {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} opened in the swamp, and the {link:horde}Horde{/link} built its first strongholds there. From the Morass it marched north and west to begin the {link:first-war}First War{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} had defeated the Horde, its soldiers came south and destroyed the Portal. The land around the gate was burned and twisted by the unmaking.
• {b}{link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde{/link}.{/b} At the urging of the archmage {link:khadgar}Khadgar{/link}, the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} raised Nethergarde Keep on the only road into the wastes. The kings of the Alliance paid for its walls.
• {b}The Portal Reopened.{/b} Some years later the gate flared to life again. {link:orcs}Orcs{/link} came through from {red:draenor}Draenor{/red} and laid siege to Nethergarde. The Alliance sent an army through the Portal after them, and the gate was destroyed a second time. The expedition did not come back.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Since then the Portal has stood cold. The Legion's remnant came to the {link:the-tainted-scar}Tainted Scar{/link} after the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, and a Horde regiment that marched into the wastes to scout it was lost almost to a man.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Wastes",
			text = [=[• It is said that no rain has ever reached the ground of the Blasted Lands. The storms that break over the eastern hills drain away into the sea before the red clay can drink.
• The beasts of the waste are unlike their kin elsewhere. A pair of elven bloodmages at the northern border hold that the energies loosed by the Portal forced them to change, and they pay well for the proof.
• Travellers who reach the swamp's southern border sometimes meet the ghost of an {link:orcs}orc{/link} who stands beside the road. He warns them to turn back. He knows what waits beyond.
• A great black drake named Teremus the Devourer is said to circle the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}. The watchers of {link:nethergarde-keep}Nethergarde{/link} count the patrols it has taken.
• Deep in the {link:the-tainted-scar}Tainted Scar{/link}, far from any road, an old human warlock called {link:daio-the-decrepit}Daio{/link} keeps an altar among the demons. He is not their prisoner.]=],
		},
	},
})

